url: "https://raspberry-kim.github.io/donghyun-lab11/"
abstract: >-
  Donghyunzooo is a browser-based, noncommercial match-three puzzle that
  follows only the Normal mode of the animal-face puzzle released as Zooo
  (Game Boy Advance, 2003) and Zoo Keeper (Nintendo DS, 2004-2005), which
  descend from a 2002-2003 browser game by Robot Communications.
  On an 8x8 board two adjacent faces are swapped; a swap that does not line
  up three or more equal faces is reverted. Each of the seven faces has a
  per-level quota, filled quotas advance the level (up to 20), and a time bar
  drains and refills as faces are captured. A wildcard face (from level 3)
  and a flashing tile that captures every face currently shown (from level
  2) appear occasionally. The only settings, the starting level (1-20) and
  the number of binocular hints (0-9; default 1 and 3), are chosen through a
  program written in the esoteric programming language Donghyun-lang.
  Keyboard, mouse/touch and gamepad input are supported. All eight faces are
  characters of the Donghyun series redrawn as 16x16 faces; no asset of the
  original games is used. The MIT license applies to the Donghyunzooo code
  and documentation; the page fonts are under the SIL Open Font License.
  See LICENSE and CREDITS.md.
keywords:
  - match-three puzzle
  - Zoo Keeper
  - esoteric programming language
  - JavaScript
